1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,120
Anthropic, the company behind Claude, has filed to go public.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,260
Ticker: ANT, on the Nasdaq.

3
00:00:07,430 --> 00:00:11,800
An IPO is the first time a private company sells shares to the public.

4
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:14,860
After that, anyone can trade them on the exchange.

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:20,950
Revenue: $16.3 billion in the first half of 2026,

6
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:25,000
and a reported $16.8 billion in the third quarter alone.

7
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:28,910
But also an $80.7 billion net loss in the first half.

8
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:36,160
The expectation: raise about $100 billion at a valuation of up to $2 trillion.

9
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:41,300
That would be the largest IPO in history, with trading possibly before Thanksgiving.

10
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:44,170
The share price is not set yet.

11
00:00:44,550 --> 00:00:49,380
It comes in an amended filing just before trading. Early estimates vary widely.

12
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:54,930
Watch the official price range, and the first day of trading.

13
00:00:55,310 --> 00:00:59,290
Shares are highly speculative. This is information, not advice.
